  "id": "tax.us.2025.rule.form1040-line25b",
  "notes": "Form 1040 line 25b: 'Add the amounts shown as federal income tax withheld' on Forms 1099-INT, 1099-DIV, 1099-R box 4, 1099-G box 4, SSA-1099 box 6, and Form 1099-B box 4 backup withholding (i1040gi-2025 line 25b). Each document's own subtotal rule is pinned and added here, one addend per document. v7: pairs Form 1099-B statements with statement-box4-withholding via require_paired, and both arms add f1099b.b4-withholding-subtotal. That subtotal is every current box 4 amount, including an amount whose statement has no sale. When no amount is recorded the subtotal is zero, and the filer is asked nothing new.",
